1
00:03:57,391 --> 00:04:03,391
The future of Kung Fu hangs in balance.

2
00:07:54,782 --> 00:08:00,782
Kung Fu Panda 2 is a animation, family, comedy film
directed by Jennifer Yuh Nelson.

3
00:11:52,173 --> 00:11:58,173
Po and his friends fight to stop a peacock villain from conquering China with a deadly
new weapon, but first the Dragon Warrior must come to terms with his past.

4
00:15:49,565 --> 00:15:55,565
Po (voice), played by Jack Black.

5
00:19:46,956 --> 00:19:52,956
Tigress (voice), played by Angelina Jolie.

6
00:23:44,347 --> 00:23:50,347
Shifu (voice), played by Dustin Hoffman.

7
00:27:41,739 --> 00:27:47,739
Lord Shen (voice), played by Gary Oldman.

8
00:31:39,130 --> 00:31:45,130
Monkey (voice), played by Jackie Chan.

9
00:35:36,521 --> 00:35:42,521
Viper (voice), played by Lucy Liu.

10
00:39:33,913 --> 00:39:39,913
Kung Fu Panda 4 is a 2024 American animated martial arts comedy film directed by Mike
Mitchell and written by Darren Lemke, Jonathan Aibel and Glenn Berger.

11
00:43:31,304 --> 00:43:37,304
The fourth film in the Kung Fu Panda franchise, it
was produced by DreamWorks Animation.

12
00:47:28,695 --> 00:47:34,695
It features Jack Black, Bryan Cranston, James Hong, Ian McShane, and
Dustin Hoffman reprising their roles from the previous films.

13
00:51:26,086 --> 00:51:32,086
In the film, Po—who must find and train his successor as the new Dragon Warrior—teams up with fox bandit Zhen to defeat
evil sorceress The Chameleon, who plans to steal the kung-fu abilities of all deceased masters in China.

14
00:55:23,478 --> 00:55:29,478
DreamWorks announced the fourth film in August 2022, with Mitchell, Stephanie Ma Stine, and
Huntley attached as director, co-director, and producer, respectively, by April 2023.

15
00:59:20,869 --> 00:59:26,869
In December 2023, most of the main voice cast, along with the return of
Aibel and Berger as writers and co-producers, were confirmed.

16
01:03:18,260 --> 01:03:24,260
Lemke's involvement was confirmed in February 2024.

17
01:07:15,652 --> 01:07:21,652
Composer Hans Zimmer, who had scored for the previous three installments,
returned as composer alongside frequent collaborator Steve Mazzaro.

18
01:11:13,043 --> 01:11:19,043
Kung Fu Panda 4 premiered at the AMC 14 Theater at The Grove in Los Angeles on March 3, 2024, and
was theatrically released in the United States on March 8 by Universal Pictures.

19
01:15:10,434 --> 01:15:16,434
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and was commercially successful, grossing $547.7 million
worldwide on an $85 million budget, outgrossing its predecessor to become the ninth-highest-grossing film of 2024.

20
01:19:07,826 --> 01:19:13,826
The film received three nominations at the 52nd Annie Awards and one
nomination at the 52nd Saturn Awards for Best Animated Feature.

21
01:23:05,217 --> 01:23:11,217
The film explores themes of mission, martial arts, kung fu, hope, villain.

22
01:27:02,608 --> 01:27:08,608
The tone is lighthearted.
